en the triangle will be:", "options": [{"text": "isosceles triangle", "added": false}, {"text": "right angled triangle", "added": false}, {"text": "obtuse angle triangle", "added": false}, {"text": "equilateral triangle", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "The marked price of a TV set is ₹18,500. If the dealer allows two successive discounts of 20% and 5%, for how much is the TV available?", "options": [{"text": "₹14,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹15,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹15,060", "added": false}, {"text": "₹14,060", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "Ajay spends of his income on different household items. If his income increases by 25% and expenditure increase by 20%, then the effect on his savings will be:", "options": [{"text": "28%", "added": false}, {"text": "61%", "added": false}, {"text": "49%", "added": false}, {"text": "35%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "A function of two variable varies directly with x and inversely with y. Determine function when x = 5 and y = 3. Given that, for x = 0 and y = 1, f = 15 and for x = 1 and y = 15, f = 2.", "options": [{"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "In how many years will ₹7,200 amount to ₹8,928 at a simple interest rate of 8% per annum?", "options": [{"text": "Four", "added": false}, {"text": "Three", "added": false}, {"text": "Two", "added": false}, {"text": "Five", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, 